<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Exceptionals boost Minorco at half year.</title>
<headline>Exceptionals boost Minorco at half year.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (US cts)  141	   vs 94</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  21	   vs same</p>
<p>    Net earnings	    317	   vs 210</p>
<p>    Net pre-exceptionals  200	   vs 210</p>
<p>    Sales		     2,770	 vs 2,415</p>
<p>    Operating earnings    342	   vs 385</p>
<p>Pre-excep earnings/share (cents) 89 vs 94</p>
<p>    Div payment date	October 30</p>
<p>    on register	     October 1</p>
<p>Full name: Minorco SA.</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said it had made net exceptional gains of $117 million from investment disposals. Analyts polled by Reuters had predicted pre-exceptional first half earnings of between $174-228 million.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
